<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT-Deutsche hikes ITT EPS view.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT-Deutsche hikes ITT EPS view.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Deutsche Morgan Grenfell Inc analyst James Murren raised 1998 estimates on ITT Corp to $4.28 per share from $3.04, citing announced and expected asset sales as it fends off a hostile bid from Hilton Hotels Corp.</p>
<p>--Kept 1997 estimate steady at $2.19 per share.</p>
<p>--Revision accounts for announced sales of Madison Square Garden properties, television station WBIS, five hotels to FelCor and expected sales of Desert Inn and Tunica casino properties.</p>
<p>--Estimates company will have raised $2.6 billion cash after sales.</p>
<p>--Expects company to use $1.25 billion to repurchase shares and $1.25 billion to reduce debt.</p>
<p>--ITT shares rose 1-1/2 to 61-1/4.</p>
<p>((--Robin Sidel, 212/859-1723))</p>
</text>
